1. AS REQUESTED IN REFTEL THE FOLLOWING ARE HOLIDAYS
TO BE CELEBRATED IN CY 1979:
BOTSWANA: JANUARY 1 (NEW YEAR'S); JANUARY 2 (PUBLIC HOLIDAY);
FEBRUARY 19 (WASHINGTON'S BIRTHDAY); APRIL 13 (GOOD FRIDAY);
APRIL 14 (SATURDAY FOLLOWING); APRIL 16 (EASTER MONDAY);
MAY 24 (ASCENSION DAY); MAY 28 (MEMORIAL DAY); JULY 4 (INDE-
PENDENCE DAY); JULY 9 (PRESIDENT'S DAY); JULY 10 (PUBLIC HOLIDAY);
SEPTEMBER 3 (LABOR DAY); SEPTEMBER 30 (BOTSWANA DAY); OCTOBER
1 (PUBLIC HOLIDAY); OCTOBER 2 (PUBLIC HOLIDAY); OCTOBER 8
(COLUMBUS DAY); NOVEMBER 12 (VETERANS DAY); NOVEMBER 22
(THANKSGIVING DAY); DECEMBER 25 (CHRISTMAS DAY); DECEMBER 26
(BOXING DAY).
NORLAND

